     "Luke next records Mary's journey to visit Elizabeth. When Elizabeth heard Mary's greeting, the child in her womb leaped, and Elizabeth was filled with the Holy Spirit. She spoke words of blessing over Mary and acknowledged the significance of the child Mary carried.",
     "Mary then responded with a song of praise. She magnified the Lord and rejoiced in God her Saviour. She spoke of God's mercy, His strength, His concern for the humble, and His faithfulness to the promises made to Abraham and his descendants.",
     "Her song reveals that her understanding of the event was connected to the larger story of God's covenant with Israel.",
     "Mary did not make herself the centre of the message. Her praise directed attention toward God, who had acted in mercy and remembered His promises.",
     "Her obedience did not mean she would never face difficulty. The wider Gospel story would bring experiences of uncertainty, danger, sorrow, and grief. Yet at this moment, she chose to respond with trust.",
     "Mary's words continue to challenge readers to consider what faithful obedience looks like when the future is not completely visible."
