     "Private Problems Do Not Always Need Public Attention\nNot every disagreement should become a public spectacle. Wise people consider what needs to be shared, with whom, and for what purpose.",
     "Be Willing to Reconsider a Decision\nJoseph's plan changed after he received the angel's message. A responsible person can revise a decision when credible new information changes the situation.",
     "A Quiet Response Is Not the Same as Ignoring a Problem\nJoseph was considering a serious course of action. His concern for Mary's dignity did not mean the situation was unimportant; it meant he wanted to handle it carefully."
