     "The Gospel does not give a detailed architectural description of the place where Jesus was born. Nor does it establish every detail of the traditional images that later developed around the nativity. The central biblical facts are that Mary gave birth, wrapped the child, and laid Him in a manger because there was no room for them in the lodging.",
