     "The shepherds were not presented as rulers or scholars with established authority. They were people who had received a message and could report what they had experienced.",
     "Their testimony demonstrates that the sharing of good news does not always begin with people who possess social influence. A person can communicate what they have learned without claiming to know everything about a subject.",
