     "text": "1. Read Luke 2:10–11, Isaiah 52:7, and Isaiah 61:1.\n2. Write down what each passage communicates about good news.\n3. Prepare a short explanation of the Christian good news in 250–350 words, centred on Jesus Christ.\n4. Make sure your explanation distinguishes God's work of salvation from promises of guaranteed wealth, comfort, or freedom from all difficulties.\n5. Practise explaining your reflection to a peer, family member, or study group in a respectful and understandable way."
