     "This detail deserves careful attention. Luke's account of Jesus' birth describes the child being laid in a manger because there was no room available for them in the lodging. Matthew later describes the wise men entering a house.",
     "The accounts need not refer to the same moment. Matthew does not say that the wise men arrived on the night of Jesus' birth, nor does he give the exact age of the child when they found Him. The common image of precisely three wise men arriving at the manger on Christmas night goes beyond what Matthew explicitly records.",
