     "Consistency Often Matters More Than Public Attention.\nCharacter develops through repeated choices. Being truthful, keeping promises, completing tasks, and treating others respectfully are important even when no one is watching.",
     "Do Not Invent Details to Make a Story More Interesting.\nA responsible study of biblical history distinguishes what Scripture records from what may be historically plausible. Respect for truth is more important than adding dramatic but unsupported details."
