   "2. Describe John's initial response to Jesus' request for baptism.",
   "3. Explain Jesus' statement about fulfilling all righteousness.",
   "4. Describe the events that took place when Jesus was baptized.",
   "5. Explain the significance of the heavens opening.",
   "6. Describe the descent of the Holy Spirit upon Jesus.",
   "7. Explain the meaning and importance of the Father's declaration from heaven.",
   "8. Identify the connections between Jesus' baptism and Old Testament prophetic themes.",
   "9. Discuss the lessons of humility, obedience, identity, and divine approval.",
   "10. Explain why Jesus' baptism is an important event in the beginning of His public ministry.",
   "Final Assignment — The Baptism of Jesus Christ",
   "Assignment Type: Comprehensive Biblical Study, Scriptural Analysis, and Personal Application",
   "Suggested Length: 1,500–2,000 words, excluding Scripture references.",
   "Objective: Demonstrate a clear understanding of the baptism of Jesus, its significance in the Gospel accounts, and its lessons concerning identity, humility, obedience, and faithful service.",
   "Part 1 — Biblical Research: The Events at the Jordan",
   "Read Matthew 3:13–17, Mark 1:9–11, and Luke 3:21–22.",
   "Write a detailed account of the baptism of Jesus.",
   "Your work should explain:",
   "1. Where Jesus came from.",
   "2. Why He came to John.",
   "3. Why John initially hesitated.",
   "4. What Jesus said about fulfilling all righteousness.",
   "5. What happened when Jesus was baptized.",
   "6. What the Spirit's descent revealed.",
   "7. What the Father's voice declared.",
   "Use appropriate Scripture references to support your explanation.",
