   "Read Matthew 3:13–17 and Matthew 5:17.",
   "Write an explanation of Jesus' statement about fulfilling all righteousness.",
   "Address the following questions:",
   "1. Why did John initially question Jesus' request?",
   "2. How did Jesus respond to John's concern?",
   "3. Why is it inappropriate to treat Jesus' baptism as an admission of personal wrongdoing?",
   "4. How does the event relate to Jesus' obedience to the Father's purpose?",
   "5. What can Christians learn about humility and obedience from this exchange?",
   "Clearly distinguish the meaning supported by the biblical passage from your own reflections.",
   "Part 3 — The Father, Son, and Holy Spirit",
   "Read Matthew 3:16–17, Mark 1:9–11, and Luke 3:21–22.",
   "Explain the significance of the three elements of the baptism narrative:",
   "A. The Son",
