   "C. The Father",
   "Explain the meaning of the Father's declaration that Jesus is His beloved Son.",
   "Conclude by explaining why this passage is important to Christian understanding of the Father, Son, and Holy Spirit.",
   "Part 4 — Old Testament Connections",
   "Read the following passages:",
   "•\tPsalm 2:7",
   "•\tIsaiah 42:1",
   "•\tIsaiah 64:1",
   "•\tMatthew 3:13–17",
   "Explain how the themes in these Old Testament passages can help readers understand Jesus' baptism.",
   "Your work should address:",
   "1. The theme of God's Son and His authority.",
   "2. The theme of God's chosen servant.",
   "3. The significance of God placing His Spirit upon His servant.",
   "4. The imagery of the heavens opening.",
   "5. How the Gospel account connects Jesus' baptism with God's wider purposes.",
   "Do not claim that every passage describes the baptism directly. Explain the thematic connections carefully and support your conclusions with Scripture.",
   "Part 5 — Comparative Study of the Gospel Accounts",
   "Prepare a comparison of Matthew 3:13–17, Mark 1:9–11, and Luke 3:21–22.",
   "Use the following framework:",
   "After completing the comparison, write a conclusion explaining how the three accounts complement one another.",
   "Remember: differences in emphasis do not automatically mean that the accounts contradict one another. Read each passage carefully and identify what each writer actually records.",
   "Part 6 — Character Study: Jesus and John",
   "Examine the actions of Jesus and John during the baptism narrative.",
   "Discuss at least five qualities or principles, including:",
   "•\tJesus' obedience.",
   "•\tJesus' humility.",
   "•\tJohn's reverence for Jesus.",
   "•\tJohn's willingness to listen and respond.",
   "•\tThe importance of understanding one's calling.",
   "•\tThe relationship between identity and responsibility.",
   "•\tThe importance of directing attention toward Christ.",
   "For each principle:",
   "1. Explain its meaning.",
   "2. Identify a relevant Scripture passage.",
   "3. Describe how it is demonstrated in the baptism narrative.",
   "4. Explain how it can be applied in everyday life.",
   "Part 7 — Personal Reflection and Practical Application",
   "Write a personal reflection responding to the following questions:",
   "1. What does Jesus' baptism teach you about obedience?",
   "2. What does John's response teach you about humility?",
   "3. How do you respond when you encounter something you do not immediately understand?",
   "4. Why is it important to distinguish genuine faithfulness from the desire for public recognition?",
   "5. What can you learn from the Father's declaration concerning Jesus' identity?",
   "6. How can you serve others faithfully without competing for attention?",
   "7. What practical change will you make as a result of studying this topic?",
   "Practical Project: Seven Days of Humility and Faithful Service",
   "Develop a seven-day plan inspired by the lessons of Jesus' baptism.",
   "Day 1 — Study the Baptism",
   "Read Matthew 3:13–17 and write down the main events.",
   "Day 2 — Practise Humility",
   "Identify one practical way to serve someone without seeking recognition.",
   "Day 3 — Choose Obedience",
   "Identify a responsibility you have been postponing and take an appropriate step toward fulfilling it.",
   "Day 4 — Become Teachable",
   "Reflect on a situation in which you need to listen more carefully or reconsider an assumption.",
   "Day 5 — Study Jesus' Identity",
   "Read John 1:29–34 and write a reflection on John's testimony concerning Jesus.",
   "Day 6 — Serve With Integrity",
   "Complete an act of service or responsibility faithfully, without exaggerating your contribution.",
   "Day 7 — Review and Commit",
   "Write down what you have learned and establish a realistic plan for continued growth.",
   "For each day, include the relevant Scripture, the action you intend to take, and a short reflection on what you learned.",
   "Assignment Submission Requirements",
   "Your final submission should include:",
   "1. A clear title and introduction.",
   "2. A detailed account of the baptism of Jesus.",
   "3. An explanation of fulfilling all righteousness.",
   "4. A study of the Father, Son, and Holy Spirit in the narrative.",
   "5. An examination of relevant Old Testament connections.",
   "6. A comparison of the three Gospel accounts.",
   "7. A character study of Jesus and John.",
   "8. A personal reflection.",
   "9. A seven-day practical application plan.",
   "10. A conclusion explaining why the baptism of Jesus is significant to Christian faith.",
   "Memory Verse",
   "Matthew 3:17 (KJV)",
   "“And lo a voice from heaven, saying, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.”",
   "Memory Reflection",
   "After memorizing this verse, reflect on these questions:",
   "1. Who spoke from heaven?",
   "2. What did the declaration reveal about Jesus?",
   "3. Why is it important to understand Jesus' identity when studying His ministry?",
   "4. How can Jesus' example of obedience influence the way you approach your own responsibilities?",
   "Closing Prayer",
   "Heavenly Father,",
   "Thank You for Your Word and for the opportunity to study the baptism of Your Son, Jesus Christ.",
   "Thank You for revealing the significance of this event through the opening of the heavens, the descent of the Holy Spirit, and Your declaration that Jesus is Your beloved Son.",
   "Help us to understand Jesus more deeply and to recognize the importance of His mission. Teach us to approach Your Word with humility, to distinguish what Scripture teaches from our own assumptions, and to grow in wisdom as we study Your truth.",
   "Lord Jesus, thank You for Your willingness to fulfil the Father's purpose. Teach us to follow Your example of humility and obedience. Help us not to consider any faithful responsibility beneath us, and give us the courage to do what is right even when we do not immediately understand every detail.",
   "Holy Spirit, guide us as we learn and apply the Word of God. Help us to grow in wisdom, faithfulness, integrity, and love. Give us the strength to serve others responsibly and the humility to recognize that our abilities and opportunities should be used for purposes greater than personal recognition.",
   "Father, teach us to value Your truth above popularity, Your approval above empty praise, and faithfulness above the desire to impress others.",
   "Help us to follow Christ more faithfully each day. May our words, decisions, relationships, and actions reflect what we learn from His life and ministry.",
   "Thank You for John's faithfulness in preparing the way and for the revelation of Jesus Christ as Your beloved Son.",
   "May our lives bring honour to You as we continue to grow in understanding, obedience, and love.",
   "In the name of Jesus Christ, our Lord and Saviour, we pray.",
   "Amen."
