     "God's Purposes Are Larger Than a Single Event.\nThe baptism introduced a ministry that would unfold through Jesus' teaching, actions, death, and resurrection.",
     "Read the Gospel Accounts With Care.\nMatthew, Mark, and Luke emphasize different aspects while reporting the central event. Comparing them helps us appreciate the full biblical presentation.",
     "The Father, Son, and Holy Spirit Are All Present in the Account.\nThe baptism provides an important passage for understanding the relationship between the Father, the Son, and the Spirit in Christian theology."
