     "Jesus also quoted the principle that God desires mercy rather than sacrifice. This reference challenged religious behaviour that emphasised outward observance while neglecting the deeper qualities God required.",
     "The meal became a demonstration of the kind of ministry Jesus was beginning to carry out. He was not merely gathering people who already enjoyed a respected reputation. He was calling people to turn toward God.",
     "The account therefore asks believers to examine how they treat people who are socially excluded, morally struggling, or unfamiliar with religious practices.",
