    "assignment": {
     "title": null,
     "text": "Read Matthew 7:13–29. Write an essay explaining how the narrow gate, the warning about false prophets, the teaching about true discipleship, and the two builders work together to communicate the importance of faithful obedience.\nDiscussion Questions — The Sermon on the Mount\nUse these questions for personal reflection, peer discussions, classroom learning, or group study.\n1. Why is the Sermon on the Mount important to understanding Jesus' message about the Kingdom of God?\n2. What does the opening setting in Matthew 5:1–2 tell us about Jesus' ministry?\n3. What does it mean to be poor in spirit?\n4. How can people mourn honestly while maintaining hope?\n5. Why is meekness different from weakness?\n6. What does it mean to hunger and thirst for righteousness?\n7. How can mercy be combined with justice and accountability?\n8. What does purity of heart involve?\n9. Why does Jesus describe peacemakers as blessed?\n10. How can believers remain faithful when they face opposition for doing what is right?\n11. What does it mean to be the salt of the earth?\n12. How can Christians become the light of the world without seeking personal praise?\n13. What did Jesus mean when He said He came to fulfil the Law and the Prophets?\n14. Why does Jesus address anger and contempt when discussing the commandment against murder?\n15. How can people pursue purity while treating others with dignity?\n16. Why does Jesus take marriage and commitment seriously?\n17. What does it mean for your yes to be yes and your no to be no?\n18. How can people reject revenge while still protecting themselves and others from harm?\n19. What does loving your enemies look like in practical situations?\n20. How can giving, prayer, and fasting become acts of hypocrisy?\n21. What does the Lord's Prayer teach about priorities, daily needs, forgiveness, and guidance?\n22. How can people use money responsibly without allowing it to become their master?\n23. What does Jesus teach about anxiety and trust in God?\n24. What is the difference between hypocritical judgment and responsible discernment?\n25. How should believers understand the instruction to ask, seek, and knock?\n26. How can the Golden Rule influence decisions in business, family life, leadership, and friendship?\n27. Why should people evaluate religious leaders by their fruit?\n28. What is the difference between calling Jesus Lord and putting His teachings into practice?\n29. What do the two builders teach about preparing for difficult seasons?\n30. Which teaching from the Sermon on the Mount most challenges your present way of living, and why?"
    }
