     "Private Fellowship Strengthens Public Service: Jesus withdrew from the crowds to pray. Time alone with God helps believers serve others without allowing activity to replace spiritual devotion.",
     "Prayer Should Be Consistent: Luke describes Jesus as frequently withdrawing to pray. Believers should develop a regular pattern of prayer rather than praying only when difficulties arise.",
     "Spiritual Priorities Require Discipline: Jesus prayed early in the morning. The central lesson is not that everyone must pray at the same hour, but that prayer deserves a protected place in daily life.",
     "Service Must Flow From Relationship With God: Christian service is not merely activity. Prayer keeps believers attentive to God and reminds them that their strength and direction depend on Him."
