     "The temple in Jerusalem was a place of worship, sacrifice, instruction, and public discussion about the things of God. During the Feast of Tabernacles, Jesus had been teaching openly, and His words had stirred strong reactions among the people. Some believed He was the promised Messiah, while others questioned His identity and authority.",
