     "John the Baptist had called people to repentance and prepared the way for Jesus’ public ministry. Elijah was remembered as a powerful prophet, and the Old Testament had spoken of Elijah’s coming in connection with the day of the Lord. Jeremiah was known for his prophetic ministry during a painful period in Judah’s history.",
     "The disciples’ answers reflected the significance people attached to Jesus. They were trying to interpret His words and works through figures they already knew from their Scriptures and traditions.",
     "Yet Jesus was not merely a repetition of an earlier prophet. His identity and mission were unique. The Gospel accounts present Him as the Christ, the Son of God, whose mission included suffering, death, and resurrection.",
