   {
    "title": "Understanding the Meaning of the Transfiguration",
    "scripture": "Matthew 17:1–8; Mark 9:2–8; Luke 9:28–36",
    "narrative": [
     "The Transfiguration was not an isolated display of supernatural power. It was a revelation that helped the disciples understand more about the identity of Jesus and the mission He had come to fulfil.",
     "The event brought together several important truths.",
     "First, Jesus was revealed in glory. His transformed appearance showed the disciples something extraordinary about the One they followed. They had known Him through His teaching, miracles, and daily interactions, but on the mountain they witnessed a remarkable manifestation of His majesty.",
     "Second, Moses and Elijah appeared and spoke with Him. Their presence connected the event with Israel’s Scriptures and history. They were important servants of God, but the Father’s declaration directed the disciples to listen to Jesus.",
     "Third, the Father identified Jesus as His beloved Son. This declaration confirmed the central place of Jesus in the event and established the importance of His words.",
     "Fourth, the conversation about Jesus’ departure at Jerusalem connected the revelation of His glory with His coming suffering. Jesus was not going to avoid the cross. His mission would proceed through suffering and death toward resurrection.",
     "Finally, the disciples were instructed to listen to Jesus. The Transfiguration was not given merely to amaze them. It was intended to deepen their understanding of the One they followed and prepare them to receive His teaching.",
     "These truths belong together. If we speak only about the glory of Jesus and ignore His suffering, we miss an essential part of the Gospel. If we speak only about His suffering and overlook His identity and glory, we also fail to appreciate the full witness of the passage.",
     "The Transfiguration reveals the glory of Jesus while directing attention to His mission.",
     "It also teaches us something about discipleship. The disciples witnessed an extraordinary moment, but they still needed to learn, receive correction, and continue following Jesus. Their journey did not end on the mountain.",
     "For believers today, the message remains clear: Jesus deserves our attention, trust, and obedience. We should learn from the Scriptures, encourage one another, and remain faithful even when we do not understand every part of God’s purposes.",
     "The mountain was a place of revelation, but the road ahead remained a place of discipleship."
    ],
    "lessons": [
     "Jesus’ Identity Is Central to the Christian Faith\nThe Transfiguration directs attention to Jesus as the beloved Son of God. Christian discipleship begins and remains centred on Him.",
     "The Scriptures Tell One Connected Story of God’s Purposes\nMoses and Elijah appeared alongside Jesus, connecting the event with Israel’s history. Understanding the wider biblical story helps us appreciate the significance of Jesus’ mission.",
     "Jesus’ Glory Must Be Understood Alongside His Suffering\nThe mountain did not remove the cross from Jesus’ path. The Gospel reveals both His glory and His willingness to suffer to accomplish His mission.",
     "Listening to Jesus Is the Proper Response to Revelation\nThe Father commanded the disciples to listen to His Son. Our response to learning about Jesus should include obedience, not merely admiration.",
     "Discipleship Continues Beyond Extraordinary Moments\nThe disciples came down from the mountain and continued following Jesus. Faithfulness is demonstrated through our ongoing response to His words in ordinary life."
    ],
    "reflections": [
     "What do you consider the most important revelation about Jesus in the Transfiguration account, and why?",
     "How does the presence of Moses and Elijah help connect the event with the wider biblical story?",
     "Why is it important to understand Jesus’ glory alongside His suffering and resurrection?",
     "What would it look like for you to obey the Father’s command to listen to Jesus this week?",
     "How can your peer group help one another apply the lessons of the Transfiguration in everyday life?"
    ],
    "assignment": {
     "title": null,
     "text": "1. What was revealed about Jesus through the Transfiguration?\n2. Who appeared with Jesus, and what does their presence connect the event to?\n3. What did the Father declare about Jesus?\n4. How does the Transfiguration relate to Jesus’ approaching suffering, death, and resurrection?\n5. What is the central lesson of the Transfiguration for Christian discipleship?"
    }
   }
