     "He continued by teaching that the person who believes in Him would live, even though that person died, and that whoever lived and believed in Him would never die in the ultimate sense expressed in His promise.",
     "These words must be understood within the wider teaching of the Gospel. Jesus was not claiming that believers would never experience physical death. Lazarus had died, and Jesus would soon call him out of the tomb. The passage distinguishes the reality of physical death from the life and hope found in Christ.",
