     "Jesus’ confrontation similarly exposed the danger of separating religious activity from faithful living.",
     "People may attend worship, participate in religious events, or contribute financially to a ministry while neglecting honesty, compassion, and justice. Religious participation cannot be used as a substitute for a life that seeks to honor God.",
     "At the same time, Jesus’ actions should not be used to justify uncontrolled anger or aggression whenever someone disagrees with us. The Gospel accounts present a specific confrontation by Jesus concerning the misuse of the temple.",
     "Believers must apply the passage with discernment, ensuring that any response to wrongdoing is guided by truth, responsibility, and a genuine desire to protect what is right."
