     "Recognize the significance of important moments.\nJesus understood the importance of this final meal. Believers should approach opportunities for fellowship, instruction, and reconciliation thoughtfully.",
     "Preparation for suffering can include serving others.\nJesus knew His suffering was approaching but still gave attention to His disciples. Difficult seasons do not eliminate the opportunity to act with love.",
     "Faithful leadership prepares others for responsibility.\nJesus used His final hours to strengthen the disciples for the work ahead. Leaders should invest in the growth of those they serve.",
     "Human weakness does not make spiritual growth impossible.\nThe disciples were not yet ready for everything they would face, but Jesus continued teaching them. Growth requires patience, correction, and dependence on God."
